  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will persist across the Great Lakes region through\nLabor Day Weekend, ushering in seasonable and less humid\nweather. Highs will reach the upper 70s to lower 80s with lows \ngenerally in the 50s, though some isolated 40s are possible, \nespecially across the interior areas Sunday night into Monday\nmorning. A few lake-enhanced showers are possible later this\nmorning and afternoon, though coverage remains uncertain given\nthe latest satellite imagery revealing large pockets of dry air\nacross the region associated with the high pressure subsidence.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nA strong upper-level trough will move east through the Upper\nGreat Lakes on Wednesday, ushering in strong warm air advection\nacross the Lower Great Lakes and Midwest. A brief period of\nheat and humidity will return across the region as heat indices\nreach the low to mid-90s in some spots Wednesday afternoon. The\nlatest guidance indicates a narrow region of instability \ndeveloping across the area in the midst of seasonably-strong mid\nand upper-level flow which could be favorable for some stronger\nstorms in the afternoon and evening, though there remains \nuncertainty on coverage. Cooler and less humid weather will\nreturn across the region Thursday into Friday as a cold front\nmoves east through the area and high pressure returns.",
